Mainline TF-A BL31 for RK3588
=============================

This directory holds a mainline ARM Trusted Firmware bl31.elf taken into the
tree, used in place of the Rockchip binary blob shipped by rkbin.

Why it exists
-------------
rockchip64_common.inc picks `BL31_PATH` for the rk3588 family:

  BRANCH == next  ->  $EXTER/packages/blobs/rockchip/rk35/
                      rk3588_bl31_tfa_v2.13.0.elf      <- this one
  otherwise       ->  $RKBIN_DIR/rk35/rk3588_bl31_v1.56.elf
                      (Rockchip's blob, TF-A v2.3 based, closed)

So the 6.18 / next branch uses mainline TF-A and legacy/current are untouched.
Nothing else needs to be toggled: u-boot's FIT packaging reads the load
addresses out of whatever ELF is handed to it via BL31=, so no u-boot change
was needed when the BL31 base moved from 0x60000 to 0x40000.

Provenance
----------
source      https://github.com/ARM-software/arm-trusted-firmware
tag         v2.13.0        (upstream, unpatched)
built with  make CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-none-linux-gnu- PLAT=rk3588 bl31
toolchain   toolchains/gcc-arm-11.2-2022.02-x86_64-aarch64-none-linux-gnu
            (gcc 11.2.1, ld 2.37)
built on    2026-09-17
md5         337a8b0abbd97623d194c6b488593b71
size        273456 bytes

rk3588 has no Cortex-M0, so M0_CROSS_COMPILE is not needed (check
plat/rockchip/rk3588/platform.mk). No ATF patches are applied - the upstream
rk3588 platform is used as-is.

ELF layout (measured on this build - see "Checking a fresh build" below)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
entry 0x40000

  paddr        FileSiz     (what decode_bl31.py writes to bl31_0x*.bin)
  0x00040000   0x01e000    <- largest, so this becomes atf-1
  0x0005e000   0x00233e
  0xff100000   0x002000

Compare with rkbin's rk3588_bl31_v1.56.elf, which has three segments with
0x00060000 (0x246cc) largest - also its entry, so the same rule held there.
Note that only FileSiz feeds the sort, not MemSiz (the 0x5e000 segment has a
large BSS: MemSiz 0x07c000).

How it reaches the board
------------------------
`BL31=` is consumed at u-boot BUILD time only, so this file needs to exist on
the build host; it is never installed into the image.

arch/arm/mach-rockchip/decode_bl31.py converts the ELF into
bl31_0x<paddr>.bin files (one per PT_LOAD segment) and fit_nodes.sh generates
u-boot.its from those filenames - so the load addresses are taken from the ELF
itself and no u-boot change is required when the BL31 base differs from
Rockchip's.

NOTE: fit_nodes.sh sorts bl31_0x*.bin by FILE SIZE, and the SPL jumps to the
`firmware` node = atf-1 = the largest segment. For this ELF the 0x40000 segment
is the largest, which is correct. If a future TF-A tag ever produces a larger
0xff100000 segment, atf-1 would be wrong and the board would hang with no
output - re-check the layout whenever this file is refreshed.

Checking a fresh build
----------------------
  readelf -h  build/rk3588/release/bl31/bl31.elf | grep Entry   # expect 0x40000
  readelf -lW build/rk3588/release/bl31/bl31.elf | grep LOAD    # 2 segments

then after a u-boot build, in u-boot/v2017.09-rk3588/:

  ls -l bl31_0x*.bin | sort --key=5 -nr   # exactly 2 files, 0x00040000 first
  grep -A6 'atf-1 {' u-boot.its           # load = <0x00040000>

Serial console (ttyS2 @ 1500000) is the only proof it actually runs: rkbin's
BL31 prints no banner, mainline TF-A prints
  NOTICE:  BL31: v2.13.0(release):v2.13.0

Refreshing
----------
Re-run the build command above, overwrite the .elf here, and update the date
and md5 fields at the top of this file.
